effective_posts.text:
@occams_razor23 @spaceghost It'll never be able to compete in the market because they deliver by law to places the other companies won't go. That's why Amazon/Temu/UPS/FedEX offload so much of their packages to USPS. That means taking on insane workloads compared to the other parcel delivery companies. 

Only recently has Amazon inched out USPS in delivering packages in 2026. That's only after another deal fell through. Before then, USPS was delivering more packages total in addition to paper mail than UPS and FexED COMBINED. 

Their workload is far beyond what FedEx and UPS have to deal with.

